<Docs slug="browse">
  <p>
    The library is a grid of thumbnails, decoded as they scroll into view, so
    a folder of several thousand photos is browsable in seconds instead of
    loading everything up front. Everything below happens with the grid in
    front of you &mdash; you never have to open a photo to rate it.
  </p>

  <h2>Rate as you go</h2>
  <p>
    The first pass through a shoot is about sorting, not editing. Give each
    photo a star rating from the stars in the bar under the grid, and the
    keepers separate from the misses before you spend time on any of them.
    Ratings are saved beside the photos, so they are still there next time
    you open the folder.
  </p>

  <h2>Build a selection</h2>
  <p>
    Click to select one photo, Shift-click to take a range, and Cmd-click to
    add or remove a single photo. The selection is
    what the bar under the grid acts on &mdash;
    <a href="/docs/adjust.html">batch adjustments</a>,
    <a href="/docs/compare-a-stack.html">stacking</a> and
    <a href="/docs/export.html">export</a> all apply to every photo in it.
  </p>
</Docs>
